      "worked": "Using the suggested grouping, the general term of the outer expansion is\n$$\\begin{align*}T_k&=\\binom{5}{k}(1+x)^{5-k}x^{2k}.\\end{align*}$$\nOnly $k=0,1,2$ can contribute to $x^4$. Their required powers from $(1+x)^{5-k}$ are $4,2,0$, respectively. The coefficient is\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=\\binom{5}{0}\\binom{5}{4}+\\binom{5}{1}\\binom{4}{2}+\\binom{5}{2}\\binom{3}{0}\\\\C&=5+30+10\\\\C&=45.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
